A||||1||Pretender||Severe power loss when cold:o(||||9||
Z||000000||Pretender||03-28-2000||01:37 AM||||for the past couple of months now when-ever it's cold outside there is absolutely no power at all when i first start up my baby. But when it's warm out side the car starts up more quickly and has almost 100% power. It almost never starts on the first turn over, but the second turn it starts right up, like i have to prime the engine or something. Could this be the "cold start injector" acting up? it runs great once i run it for a while and tramp the gas but when-ever it's cold my nikes' run a better 1/4 time......help?<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||ka4nkf||03-29-2000||05:22 PM||||The cold start switch only works during starter engagement, so I don't think it would be it. Check the MAT sensor in the air cleaner. This sensor tells the ECM what the air temp is and to give it more or less gas.<BR>Check with OHM meter.<BR>210 deg. heat you should read 185 OHMS<BR>160 deg heat you should read 450 OHMS<BR>100 deg heat you should read 1800 OHMS<BR> 70 deg heat you should read 3400 OHMS<BR> 40 deg heat you should read 7500 OHMS<BR> 20 deg heat you should read 13,500 OHMS<BR>  0 deg heat you should read 25,000 OHMS<BR>-40 deg heat you should read 100,700 OHMS<BR>I found out if you unplug the connector and install a 10,000 OHM resister it runs good.<BR>It fools the computer and makes it think it is cold, therefore giving it more gas. It works for me , runs good.||||reg||1
